This work investigates the application of fractional-order low-pass filters to electroencephalographic (EEG) signal analysis.

Two non-integer-order low-pass filters were evaluated and compared with conventional Butterworth filtering. The study explores fractional-order filtering as an alternative signal-processing approach for complex biomedical signals such as EEG.

